A3.3 -- M-b isolated: sigma divisor frozen at the clean latent
==============================================================================
  Shipped chain divides by sigma(L_observed). Freezing the divisor at
  sigma(L_latent) removes mechanism M-b and leaves M-a alone.

  arm                       SD mean     SD med       p05       p95  IQR/med      rho
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  M62/shipped              0.018006   0.017994  0.013109  0.022893   0.2209   1.1835
  M62/frozen-divisor       0.017721   0.017756  0.012713  0.022555   0.2266   1.1647
    -> M-b contributes +1.61% of rho on M62  (shipped 1.1835 vs frozen 1.1647)

  coffee-bean/shipped      0.012671   0.012674  0.007379  0.017766   0.3395   0.8329
  coffee-bean/frozen-divisor   0.012622   0.012627  0.007343  0.017682   0.3411   0.8297
    -> M-b contributes +0.39% of rho on coffee-bean  (shipped 0.8329 vs frozen 0.8297)

==============================================================================
A3.4 -- M66's frozen-eta latent, priced on the curve
==============================================================================
  A real frame is T + eta. M66's REAL replicate is T + eta_0 + eps, so its
  latent carries E|grad eta|^2 = 2 s^2 of gradient that a real frame's
  latent does not. On the operator's own scale that inflates nu^2 by 2 s^2,
  i.e. z_M66^2 = z_true^2 + 2.

